  "why": "The ONE exception to family-mismatch-must-reject: the records share an identity Alt ID (same Kind+Value, relation absent or IsSameAs). A misassigned season keeps its external ids, so a shared identity id is the one signal that outranks recorded ancestry -- the pair may surface for a human. It may NOT auto-accept: the ancestry disagreement is exactly what the reviewer must resolve. verdict_in [Review] pins both walls at once. The exception requires a CLEAN identity match; a shared id alongside a conflicting id on another source rejects, because a genuinely misassigned record keeps its ids consistently.",
